==========================================================================
 LAS parameter set: n=6 ell=5 kappa=49 gamma=137984  (d=256, Q=8380417)
   M = n + ell = 11   (dim of sk=r, witness r', mask y, responses z_hat/z)
   paper notation: pp=(A,H)  pk=t  sk=r  statement Y=t'  witness r'
   signing mask y -> commitment w = A*y  (hashed into c; NOT transmitted)
==========================================================================
 Reproducibility: compiler=13.3.0
                  built=Aug 28 2026 12:44:33   git=n/a (n/a)
                  (CPU / OS-WSL / run-date captured per run by
                   scripts/run_fair_benchmarks.sh into metadata.txt)
 5 repetitions x 500 (sign-class) / 1000 (verify-class) iters/op; mean +/- sample SD;
 single thread, -O3.  Repetition scheme, fixed pp seed and fixed 33-byte message
 mirror the Rust driver (rust/fips204-las/examples/bench_levels.rs) exactly.
 Cycles/op via upstream test/cpucycles.{h,c} (rdtsc; invariant-TSC reference
 cycles), read once per repetition window: measured read overhead 1 cycles,
 i.e. ~0.0020 cycles/op at the 500-iteration sign-class loop -- negligible, not
 subtracted.  One setup and one consistent state per run (plus its packed byte
 image for the end-to-end tier); primary protocol timings first, then
 diagnostics from the SAME state (cost-attribution / communication aids).

--- WHAT IS COMPARED (separate base/adaptor modules; matched parameters; shared primitives) ---
 BASE  (simplified Dilithium-style signature; NO adaptor statement t'):
   Sign      c = H(pk, w,      M)        Verify    c == H(pk, w',      M)
 LAS ADAPTOR (same scheme; statement/lock Y=t' folded into the hash):
   PreSign   c = H(pk, w + t', M),  z_hat = y + c*r  (reject |z_hat|inf > gamma-kappa-1)
   PreVerify c == H(pk, w' + t', M)
   Adapt     z = z_hat + r'   (final response z;          reject |z|inf > gamma-kappa)
   Ext       s = z - z_hat   (recovers the witness r')
   Adapted sig clears ordinary Verify without an explicit +t' because
     A(z_hat + r') - c*t = (A*z_hat - c*t) + A*r' = w' + t'   (t' = A*r').
   pi (paper-level off-chain proof of well-formedness) is NOT implemented/measured here.
 Every operation is timed at BOTH API tiers: TIER 1 core crypto (structs in/out,
 pure computation) and TIER 2 end-to-end packed (bytes in/out; validating
 unpack -> core -> pack inside the call, upstream sign.c's boundary).

##########################################################################
# PRIMARY (protocol-level) timings -- the headline adaptor-overhead table #
##########################################################################
--- COMPUTATION, TIER 1: CORE CRYPTO (struct API; pure computation, no codec)
    (per op: microseconds AND cycles, each mean +/- sample SD) ---

 Shared (public params pp=(A,H); KeyGen -> pk=t, sk=r):
   Setup             43.05 +/-   0.72 us       154673 +/-      2582 cyc
   KeyGen            44.40 +/-   1.41 us       159529 +/-      5055 cyc

 Base path (simplified Dilithium-style, c = H(pk, w, M); no t'):
   Sign             403.18 +/-  17.25 us      1448696 +/-     61979 cyc
   Verify            91.57 +/-   0.51 us       329040 +/-      1831 cyc

 LAS adaptor path (statement t' folded into the hash, c = H(pk, w+t', M)):
   PreSign          412.19 +/-   9.88 us      1481059 +/-     35499 cyc
   PreVerify         96.24 +/-   1.57 us       345798 +/-      5650 cyc
   Adapt             98.32 +/-   0.87 us       353292 +/-      3121 cyc
   Ext               35.92 +/-   0.48 us       129047 +/-      1719 cyc

 Adaptor overhead (adaptor op vs the base op it mirrors; core tier, us):
   PreSign       vs Sign       412.19 vs   403.18   (+2.2%)
   PreVerify     vs Verify      96.24 vs    91.57   (+5.1%)
   Adapt         vs Verify      98.32 vs    91.57   (+7.4%)
   Ext (separate)               35.92            (no base analogue)

--- COMPUTATION, TIER 2: END-TO-END PACKED (byte API: validating unpack ->
    core -> pack INSIDE the call -- the boundary upstream sign.c exposes;
    same repetition scheme and units; Setup has no packed twin) ---

 Shared:
   KeyGen_packed      145.84 +/-   0.21 us       524043 +/-       754 cyc

 Base path (bytes in/out):
   Sign_packed        641.84 +/-  35.70 us      2306234 +/-    128280 cyc
   Verify_packed      319.51 +/-  14.76 us      1148038 +/-     53020 cyc

 LAS adaptor path (bytes in/out; las_verify_packed = the on-chain-style entry):
   PreSign_packed     743.29 +/-   9.05 us      2670771 +/-     32504 cyc
   PreVerify_packed   440.65 +/-   2.53 us      1583350 +/-      9081 cyc
   Adapt_packed       589.27 +/-   9.32 us      2117340 +/-     33474 cyc
   Ext_packed         445.15 +/-   2.97 us      1599491 +/-     10656 cyc

 Adaptor overhead at the packed boundary (adaptor op vs base op, us):
   PreSign_packed   vs Sign_packed      743.29 vs   641.84   (+15.8%)
   PreVerify_packed vs Verify_packed    440.65 vs   319.51   (+37.9%)
   Adapt_packed     vs Verify_packed    589.27 vs   319.51   (+84.4%)
   Ext_packed (separate)                445.15            (no base analogue)
   NOTE: these packed-boundary overheads fold in EXTRA CODEC WORK, not just
   adaptor math -- PreSign_packed/PreVerify_packed additionally decode the
   pk-sized statement t'; Adapt_packed additionally decodes t' and the witness
   r' and re-packs the adapted signature.  The CORE tier above isolates the
   pure adaptor computation (the headline overhead); the codec-cost table
   below prices the byte boundary itself.

 Codec boundary cost (packed minus core, per op, us -- the price of the
 byte boundary: validating unpack of the inputs + pack of the output;
 differences of independently measured means, so small values sit within
 the SDs above):
   KeyGen_packed    - KeyGen        +101.45   (+228.5%)
   Sign_packed      - Sign          +238.66   ( +59.2%)
   Verify_packed    - Verify        +227.93   (+248.9%)
   PreSign_packed   - PreSign       +331.10   ( +80.3%)
   PreVerify_packed - PreVerify     +344.42   (+357.9%)
   Adapt_packed     - Adapt         +490.94   (+499.3%)
   Ext_packed       - Ext           +409.23   (+1139.4%)

